From: acqxi <kacqxi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:21:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 05/15] Performance metrics: turn timing, its contract and
 settings

Adds OrchestrationV2TurnPerformance to the provider turn contract and the
Stats for nerds settings (hidden metrics, composer and per-reply switches).

Adds a provider-agnostic TurnPerformanceTracker (provider-core) and feeds it
from the Claude, Codex and ACP adapters, emitting
OrchestrationV2ProviderTurn.performance on provider_turn.updated: a live
snapshot at the first token and at the first answer, and the final value at
the terminal update. One tracker per provider turn; nothing carries across
turns, sessions or process replacements.

- TTFT ends at the first generated token (reasoning, answer, tool-call
  arguments); tool lifecycle events never end it. TTFA needs non-whitespace
  answer text.
- Generation windows close at a tool start, response boundary or approval
  wait; generationMs sums them. Claude counts exact message_delta tokens for
  fully observed messages; Codex and ACP spread the turn's exact output over
  the windows, else chars/4.
- Peak tokens/s over full 2 s windows (100 ms buckets), calibrated to an
  exact count when the ratio is plausible; omitted below 2 s of generation.
- Tools: wall-clock union, count, longest, open calls (partial).
- ProjectionStore and the client projection keep the latest measurement,
  and a live snapshot never replaces a terminal one.
- OrchestrationV2ProviderTurnJson maps performance.requestSentAt to an ISO
  string so the measurement survives persistence and the wire.
